 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Logic function",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Each of the six channels is a non-inverting buffer: nY is HIGH when nA is HIGH and LOW when nA is LOW."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Schmitt-trigger inputs",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "An input switches the output HIGH on crossing VT+ while rising and LOW only on falling below VT-; the gap VH between them keeps a slow or noisy edge from making the output chatter. At VCC = 3.0 V, VT+ is at most 2.2 V, VT- at least 0.9 V and VH between 0.3 V and 1.2 V. Input edges may be as slow as 50 ms/V at 2.3 V to 2.7 V, 20 ms/V at 3.0 V to 3.6 V and 1 ms/V at 4.5 V to 5.5 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Supply current during a transition",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "While an input sits between the rails, supply current rises well above the static 2 µA: typically about 1.3 mA peak at VCC = 3.0 V, 2.9 mA at 4.5 V and 4 mA at 5.5 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Overvoltage-tolerant inputs",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Inputs take 0 V to 5.5 V in operation, at any VCC from 1.8 V to 5.5 V, so a signal from a higher supply domain can drive a lower-voltage device. The absolute limit on an input is 7.0 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Partial power-down (IOFF)",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "With VCC at 0 V the outputs are turned off, so no current flows back through the device from signals still present. In that state inputs and outputs may sit anywhere from GND to 5.5 V with at most 0.5 µA leakage at 25 °C, 5 µA over temperature."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output drive",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "At VCC = 3.0 V an output sinks or sources 8 mA with VOL at most 0.36 V and VOH at least 2.58 V at 25 °C; at VCC = 4.5 V it handles 16 mA with VOL at most 0.44 V and VOH at least 3.94 V. Absolute output current is ±50 mA per pin, 100 mA total into VCC."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching noise",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "With 50 pF loads at VCC = 3.3 V a quiet LOW output typically bounces to 0.3 V peak (0.8 V max) and a quiet HIGH output dips to about 3.0 V. At 5.0 V the figures are 0.6 V peak LOW and 4.5 V HIGH valley."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Robustness",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Latch-up immunity is over 250 mA (JESD 78 Class II). ESD withstand is over 3000 V HBM (JS-001 class 2) and over 2000 V CDM (JS-002 class C3)."
  }
 ],
